<title>ARGENTINA: Argentine union chief calls strike a success.</title>
<headline>Argentine union chief calls strike a success.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>The head of Argentina's CGT labor federation called Thursday's general strike a success, saying industry in the capital was completely paralized.</p>
<p>&quot;It is already a success,&quot; Rodolfo Daer told local radio. &quot;There are more buses in the streets than people.&quot;</p>
<p>The CGT called its third general strike this year in reaction to President Carlos Menem's decision to decree measures designed to make labor markets more flexible last week. Unions say the decrees reduce workers' rights.</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
